{"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The IvorTiming framework provides musical time, duration, and tempo types","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written in Swift. Both beat-based (measured in whole notes) and wall-clock","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"representations of time and duration are supported, along with tempo-based","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"types for converting between the two and a quantizer for snapping beat times to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rhythmic grid points.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import IvorTiming","","var tempoMap = TempoMap()","","tempoMap.insert(beatTime: 0, tempo: Tempo(120))     \/\/ ♩ = 120","tempoMap.insert(beatTime: 2, tempo: Tempo(60))      \/\/ slow to ♩ = 60 over two whole notes","","tempoMap[1].plain                           \/\/ \"1\/4=105\" (♩ = 105)","","let converter = TimeConverter(tempoMap: tempoMap)","","converter.wallTime(at: 1).plain             \/\/ \"2.090202\" (seconds)","converter.beatTime(at: WallTime(doubleValue: 2)!).plain    \/\/ \"0.96\" (whole notes)","","let quantizer = try BeatQuantizer(factors: [16, 12])","","quantizer.quantize(BeatTime(plain: \"0.33\")!).plain  \/\/ \"0 1\/3\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTiming\/documentation\/IvorTiming\/UsingIvorTiming","isActive":true},{"text":" for a full guide to times and durations, tempo maps,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conversion, quantization, and error handling.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortiming"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorTiming\/docum